  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do -- can a proviso such as this extend more broadly than -- than your -- than this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But, if so, they can say that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Can I just ask you about your point that we should not reach the Supremacy Clause question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: And so I guess I don't understand that -- you know, I appreciate that we could also hear that question, but I'm a little worried about suggesting that we can exercise jurisdiction to resolve a question that never appeared -- only a question that never appeared any -- in any cert petition before us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Mr. Mills, to be clear, the Eleventh Circuit is the only circuit that has adopted this particular line of thinking with respect to these kinds of cases, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first thing I'd like to point out along the lines of what Justice Sotomayor was asking is that the government's position in this case and the Eleventh Circuit's decision below, their understanding of the discretionary-function exception would do two things. One, it would eat up almost all of the entire FTCA, but, two, more importantly, it would certainly eat up all the claims that the proviso was enacted to provide liability for."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae8402906c3f6b8a66be948faae8f08b6932b93d4d98c8f81904d14e8c4aa7c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae8402906c3f-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
